<title>UK: SQUASH-FITZGERALD TAKES OVER FROM MARTIN AS NUMBER ONE.</title>
<headline>SQUASH-FITZGERALD TAKES OVER FROM MARTIN AS NUMBER ONE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>New World Open champion Sarah Fitz-Gerald has ended the 3-1/2-year reign of fellow-Australian Michelle Martin as the number one in women's squash.</p>
<p>Fitz-Gerald did not drop a game on the way to clinching her world title in Kuala Lumpur this month. Then she helped Australia retain the team title.</p>
<p>Martin is second while England's Cassie Jackman, winner of the Tournament of Champions in New York on Monday in which she beat Martin for the second time in a month, moves up to third place.</p>
<p>Top 10 rankings:</p>
<p>1. Sarah Fitz-Gerald (Australia)</p>
<p>2. Michelle Martin (Australia)</p>
<p>3. Cassie Jackman (England)</p>
<p>4. Suzanne Horner (England)</p>
<p>5. Sue Wright (England)</p>
<p>6. Liz Irving (Australia)</p>
<p>7. Carol Owens (Australia)</p>
<p>8. Sabine Schoene (Germany)</p>
<p>9. Claire Nitch (South Africa)</p>
<p>10. Fiona Geaves (England)</p>
</text>
